*** Keywords ***
General_SiSo_Auto_eCPRI_Fronthaul_Delay_Online_Activated_Deactivated_with_L3call
    [Documentation]  Test verifies whether the activation and deactivation of the eCPRI fronthaul one-way delay measurement feature do not affect the
    ...              L3 call and verifies the visibility and correctness of the periodic measurements in the syslog.
    ...              All steps:
    ...              1. Activate the eCPRI fronthaul one-way delay measurement (CB009301).
    ...              2. Perform L3 call.
    ...              3. Wait for a specified time to collect more periodic measurements not disturbed by the cell(s) reconfiguration 
    ...                 and L3 call (block/unblock cells). By default, wait for 5 minutes.
    ...              4. Validate periodic measurements in the Syslog.
    ...                 4.1. Validate measurements from feature activation to the end of the L3 call, allowed invalid response result.
    ...                 4.2. Validate measurements from the end of the L3 call to the end of the test, not allowed invalid response result.
    ...                 4.3  Validate measurement sessions if detected equal expected.
    ...              5. Deactivate the eCPRI fronthaul one-way delay measurement.
    ...              6. Perform L3 call.
    ...              7. Validate periodic measurements from the feature deactivation to the end of the L3 call.
    ...              8. Repeat steps 1-4.

    ...              ARGS:
    ...                !!! IMPORTANT !! When executing test case with L3 call, if your testline is connected to programmable
    ...                                 attenuator please ensure that all relevant ports are unattenuated as this test case
    ...                                 will not handle attenuation.
    ...                - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for each cell identified by
    ...                               its nrCellIdentity for NR cells, eutranCellId for LTE cells, wnCelId for WCDMA cells.
    ...                               Example:
    ...                               {
    ...                                   '827736065':
    ...                                        {
    ...                                            'throughput':
    ...                                                {
    ...                                                    'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                    'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                },
    ...                                            'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                        },
    ...                               }
    ...                - cells_distnames: CONFIGURATION distnames of cells that will be called.
    ...                                   If not given, list of all cells on testline will be determined and called.
    ...                - protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...                - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...                - tput_verification_via_btslog: True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                                False - throuput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...                - ue_network_modes: dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}.
    ...                                    Possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE.
    ...                                    When using more than one UE, please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                    with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                    Mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None.
    ...                - ues_and_cells: dict with UE serial numbers and lists of configuration distnames of cells to which they
    ...                                 can be attached e.g. {"SN1234": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-1", "MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-3"],
    ...                                                       "SN5678": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-5"]}
    ...                                 defaults to ${None} which means that all UEs will be attached to all cells.
    ...                                 When given, listed cells will be called in pairs with specified UEs, if there are more
    ...                                 cells on the setup that were not mentioned in the list, they will be called with all UEs
    ...                - prepare_cells_to_call: True - cells will be prepared for L3 call (blocked/barred) before the L3 call
    ...                - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                List of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred.
    ...                - wait_after_l3call: time to wait after L3 call in seconds to collect additional periodic measurements
    ...                  not disturbed by the L3 call (block/unblock cells); defaults to 300
    ...                - wait_after_parameter_change: time to wait after changing the 'actEcpriDelayMeasurement' parameter 
    ...                  in seconds; defaults to 15

    [Arguments]      ${throughputs}
    ...              ${cells_distnames}=${None}
    ...              ${protocol}=udp
    ...              ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...              ${tput_verification_via_btslog}=${False}
    ...              ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...              ${ues_and_cells}=${None}
    ...              ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...              ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}
    ...              ${wait_after_l3call}=300
    ...              ${wait_after_parameter_change}=30
    [Timeout]        24 hours
    
    ${bts_type}=                                        hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    ${connection_alias}=                                connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                                 bts_type=${bts_type}
    Set test variable                                   ${connection}    ${connection_alias}

    swconfig_operations.verify_swconfig_flags           flags=0x10040=1
    ...                                                 bts_type=${bts_type}

    config_operations.connect                           alias=${connection}
    ${initial_parameter_value}=                         config_operations.get_parameter_value
    ...                                                 dist_name=MRBTS-{}/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/FEATCADM-1
    ...                                                 param_name=actEcpriDelayMeasurement

    FOR  ${feature_activated}                           IN    true    false    true
        Set actEcpriDelayMeasurement Parameter          parameter_value=${feature_activated}
        ...                                             connection=${connection}
        ${start_time}=                                  get_local_datetime
        Robot Log Operation                             Parameter change may have caused a reset of the cells. Waiting for onAir...
        sleep                                           ${wait_after_parameter_change}
        Wait Until Keyword Succeeds                     10min     5 sec
        ...                                             Check statuses of all cells
        ...                                             connection=${connection}
        
        Robot Log Operation                             Executing L3 call with parameter actEcpriDelayMeasurement='${feature_activated}'...
        Execute L3 call                                 throughputs=${throughputs}
        ...                                             cells_distnames=${cells_distnames}
        ...                                             protocol=${protocol}
        ...                                             udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                                             tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
        ...                                             ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
        ...                                             ues_and_cells=${ues_and_cells}
        ...                                             prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
        ...                                             ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}
        ${stop_time_after_l3call}=                      get_local_datetime
        
        IF   '${feature_activated}'=='true'
            ${msg}=                                     Catenate  Waiting for ${wait_after_l3call}s to collect additional periodic measurements
            ...                                         not disturbed by L3call (block/unblock cells).
            Robot Log Operation                         ${msg}
            Sleep                                       ${wait_after_l3call}
            ${stop_time}=                               get_local_datetime
        ELSE
            ${stop_time}=                               Set Variable  ${stop_time_after_l3call}
        END

        Verify Periodic Measurements                    measurements_visible=${feature_activated}
        ...                                             start_time=${start_time}
        ...                                             stop_time_after_l3call=${stop_time_after_l3call}
        ...                                             stop_time=${stop_time}
        Robot Log Operation                             Test with with parameter actEcpriDelayMeasurement='${feature_activated}' finished successfully.\n
    END
    Robot Log Operation                                 Test finished successfully.
        
    [Teardown]                                          eCPRI Fronthaul Online_Activated_Deactivated Teardown
    ...                                                 bts_type=${bts_type}
    ...                                                 initial_parameter_value=${initial_parameter_value}


Verify Periodic Measurements
    [Documentation]    Verify whether periodic measurements are visible in the syslog as specified by feature activation status.
    [Arguments]        ${measurements_visible}
    ...                ${start_time}
    ...                ${stop_time_after_l3call}
    ...                ${stop_time}

    ${syslog_paths}=                                    btslog_parser.get_all_btslog_files_path
    IF    '${measurements_visible}'=='true'
        Check If Periodic Measurements Are Visible      syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
        ...                                             start_time=${start_time}
        ...                                             stop_time_after_l3call=${stop_time_after_l3call}
        ...                                             stop_time=${stop_time}
    ELSE
        Check If Periodic Measurements Are Not Visible  syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
        ...                                             start_time=${start_time}
        ...                                             stop_time=${stop_time}
    END


Check If Periodic Measurements Are Visible
    [Documentation]    Verify whether periodic measurements are visible in the syslog and if they are correct.
    ...                All checks:
    ...                1. Check if the number of created sessions in one measurement is equal to the expected number of sessions
    ...                2. Check if all created sessions have response with result. After L3 call the result should be 'ok'.
    ...                3. Check if the time difference from 'create sessions' in the actual and previous session is < 61 seconds.
    ...                4. Check if detected and expected number of sessions are equal.
    
    [Arguments]        ${syslog_paths}
    ...                ${start_time}
    ...                ${stop_time_after_l3call}
    ...                ${stop_time}
    ${msg}=                                             Catenate  Validating periodic measurements from time range: ${start_time.strftime("%H:%M:%S")} 
    ...                                                 - ${stop_time_after_l3call.strftime("%H:%M:%S")}. Invalid response results are allowed.
    Robot Log Operation                                 ${msg}
    btslog_verifiers.verify_periodic_ecipri_delay_measurements     
    ...                                                 syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
    ...                                                 start_time=${start_time}
    ...                                                 stop_time=${stop_time_after_l3call}
    ...                                                 connection=${connection}
    ...                                                 logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                                 measurements_activated=${True}
    ...                                                 allow_nok_result=${True}
         
    ${msg}=                                             Catenate  Validating periodic measurements after L3call time range: ${stop_time_after_l3call.strftime("%H:%M:%S")}
    ...                                                 - ${stop_time.strftime("%H:%M:%S")}. Invalid response results are NOT allowed.
    Robot Log Operation                                 ${msg}
    btslog_verifiers.verify_periodic_ecipri_delay_measurements      
    ...                                                 syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
    ...                                                 start_time=${stop_time_after_l3call}
    ...                                                 stop_time=${stop_time}
    ...                                                 connection=${connection}
    ...                                                 logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                                 measurements_activated=${True}
    ...                                                 allow_nok_result=${False}

    Robot Log Operation                                 Validating periodic measurement sessions
    btslog_verifiers.verify_detected_equals_expected_periodic_sessions
    ...                                                 syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
    ...                                                 start_time=${start_time}
    ...                                                 stop_time=${stop_time}


Check If Periodic Measurements Are Not Visible
    [Documentation]    Verify whether periodic measurements are not visible in the syslog.
    [Arguments]        ${syslog_paths}
    ...                ${start_time}
    ...                ${stop_time}
    
    ${msg}=                                             Catenate  Validating periodic measurements from time range: ${start_time.strftime("%H:%M:%S")} 
    ...                                                 - ${stop_time.strftime("%H:%M:%S")}. Periodic measurements should not be visible in syslog.
    Robot Log Operation                                 ${msg}

    btslog_verifiers.verify_periodic_ecipri_delay_measurements      
    ...                                                 syslog_paths=${syslog_paths}
    ...                                                 start_time=${start_time}
    ...                                                 stop_time=${stop_time}
    ...                                                 connection=${connection}
    ...                                                 logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                                 measurements_activated=${False}


eCPRI Fronthaul Online_Activated_Deactivated Teardown
    [Documentation]    Test Teardown keyword restoring parameter actEcpriDelayMeasurement to initial.
    [Arguments]        ${bts_type}
    ...                ${initial_parameter_value}

    Restore Parameter actEcpriDelayMeasurement To Initial
    ...                                                 initial_parameter_value=${initial_parameter_value}